已完成
- 验证证据有效；用户可见收益尚未声明。
- 验收标准（Contract 原文） / Acceptance criteria (Contract language)
- A1: Preserve original WI-1087 HEAD and all eleven protected raw file hashes including P1 sources and sequence5; no real recovery is performed by this implementation work item.
- A2: After a real current native human gate, reproduce the actual pre-fix discontinuity in a fresh temporary Git repository before implementing the fix; preserve exact RED output and transaction phase evidence.
- A3: The forward native activation writer records actual A/B repository WI owner Runtime and journal bindings with prepared/committed evidence. Only state not_ready-to-implementation_active, observed baseRevision and observed repositorySnapshotDigest may change; any other unamended human-plan change rejects.
- A4: Legacy recovery is a separate current-baseline request and real human decision/record. Enumerate the exact finite fields and pre-first-checkpoint stage plus old/new differences and retained historical unknowns. An old B review or arbitrary CSV match never authenticates A-to-B.
- A5: A valid present recovery record enables only generation of fresh preflight. It does not approve current C, grant business authority, rewrite history, backdate a receipt or reuse an old review as a new human decision.
- A6: Validate every existing record and the prospective complete chain before publishing a new transaction under current ownership/CAS. Wrong incoming requests must not finish unrelated pending operations; prepared-only or partial evidence never counts as committed.
- A7: Preserve existing journal/hash/sequence checks and rehashed-discontinuous tests. Reject missing start/checkpoint bindings, foreign identity/owner, extra scope/authority/actor/source changes, unexplained post-checkpoint gaps, stale request/history/summary/registration, CAS and pending/partial failures.
- A8: The original twelve reviewed Rust paths implement shared repository recovery APIs, strict standalone protocol types, bounded metadata admission and explicit CLI/MCP plan-record surfaces. One additional Rust test path, crates/cockpit-mcp/tests/rpc.rs, changes only its exact discovery names and count from the actual baseline33 to35. No new Contract root field, production feature or hidden controls bypass.
- A9: Preserve exact MCP tool counts and existing usage/material-review assertions. With exactly two recovery tools added to actual baseline 33 assert exactly 35 and exact names plus strict schemas; never weaken to a lower bound or delete count assertions.
- A10: Update three-language commands and own briefs consistently. Only append/update WI-1088 actual-stage rows in the three reference-parity files; retain all other WI conclusions unchanged and mark unrun acceptance honestly.
- A11: Run all declared checks with one worker, isolated target and each command node at most 900 seconds; preserve actual formal results and CI for the exact pushed HEAD. No success is inferred from old WI evidence.
- A12: Normal bounded phase commit/push and existing Draft PR1047 updates are authorized. No merge, close, deletion, Runtime installation, direct-main push, P2a/P2b, live grant, Sentinel operation or real WI-1087 recovery.

